From 3bd2f366b3d88721ebebf24b5a933f65b83ef728 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leon Bollerup <mail@r2x2.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 19:49:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] QAT-aware Q4_0: recover each block's BF16 QAT grid and store
 it exactly

- ggml quantize_q4_0 (GGML_Q4_0_QAT=1) and gguf-py Q4_0 (GGUF_Q4_0_QAT=1): s is
  bf16(amax / k) for the k in 1..8 that puts every weight on an integer in
  [-8, 7]; off-grid blocks keep the reference encoder.
- convert_hf_to_gguf: --outtype q4_0 (writes Q4_0 directly, no BF16 GGUF step).
Gemma 4 31B QAT assistant: 100% of blocks on the grid, 0.2% vs 5% relative error.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 conversion/base.py     |  2 ++
 convert_hf_to_gguf.py  |  3 +-
 ggml/src/ggml-quants.c | 65 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 gguf-py/gguf/quants.py | 46 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 115 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

